# Written by the unit-test JVM: the test JVM's working directory is the repo root, so
# CommandsSpyConfig.load() creates a default commands-spy.json under <repo>/config, and
# log4j-core writes logs/latest.log. Neither is build output, so /build does not cover them.
/config/commands-spy.json
/logs/

# fabric-loader 0.19.3 writes its own log during fabric-loader-junit runs
fabricloader.log

# neoforge/ is a standalone Gradle build, so the root-anchored /build above does
# not cover its output tree - and that tree is multi-GB: ModDevGradle caches the
# decompiled and recompiled Minecraft under it.
neoforge/build/
